---
---

<section class="relative py-20 sm:py-28 lg:py-32 bg-muted/50">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      {/* Eyebrow */}
      <div class="mb-8">
        <span class="inline-block text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">
          Why RDS 81346
        </span>
      </div>

      {/* Section Heading */}
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-16 leading-tight">
        Bring clarity to every level of engineering.
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-16">
        A structured approach to engineering does more than organize components. It creates a shared
        understanding of complex systems, making information easier to find, communicate, and manage.
      </p>

      {/* Benefits Grid */}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-16">
        {/* Benefit 1 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">01</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Structure complexity</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>Make complex systems easier to understand.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Break down large technical systems into clear, manageable hierarchies. From entire facilities
                to individual components, RDS 81346 provides a consistent way to organize and navigate system
                structures.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Benefit 2 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">02</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Speak the same language</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>One reference system. Every discipline.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Electrical, mechanical, process, and other engineering disciplines often describe the same
                systems differently. RDS 81346 establishes a shared reference model, allowing teams to
                collaborate without losing their discipline-specific perspectives.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Benefit 3 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">03</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Identify with confidence</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>Give every object a clear identity.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Create consistent reference designations for systems, equipment, and components. Standardized
                identification reduces ambiguity and helps ensure everyone refers to the same object across
                drawings, documentation, and engineering tools.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Benefit 4 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">04</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Connect engineering information</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>Keep information connected to what it describes.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Link engineering data, documentation, and technical objects through a common system structure.
                Improve traceability and establish a stronger foundation for information exchange between
                tools, teams, and organizations.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Benefit 5 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">05</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Think beyond the design phase</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>A structure that lasts throughout the lifecycle.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Engineering information remains valuable long after a project is delivered. RDS 81346 supports
                continuity from design and construction to operation, maintenance, and future modifications.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Benefit 6 */}
        <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start space-x-4">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary flex-shrink-0">06</span>
            <div class="flex-1">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Build for what comes next</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                <strong>A foundation for digital engineering.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mt-3">
                Consistent structures and reference designations make engineering information easier to reuse,
                integrate, and manage digitally. Establish the groundwork for model-based engineering,
                automation, and connected asset information.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
